    "title": "How many students were enrolled in Green County Monroe School District in 2023-24 school year?",
    "text": "Juda School District Superintendent Traci Davis (2023) | Juda School District\nJuda School District Superintendent Traci Davis (2023) | Juda School District\nWisconsin Department of Public Instruction.\nOf all the students welcomed in the 2023-24 school year, 53% of them were boys, and 47% were girls.\nData also showed that most of the students were white, representing 96.1% of the Monroe School District's total enrollment.\nAmong the six districts in Green County, Brodhead School District ranked second in enrollment numbers with 1,017 students, while New Glarus School District welcomed 957 students and ranked third in the 2023-24 school year.\nMonroe School District roughly covers schools within Green County, with its main office in Monroe.\nIn the previous school year, Monroe School District also had the highest number of students among Green County districts.\nNearly 830,000 students were enrolled in Wisconsin schools in the 2021-22 school year. This is a 0.85% decrease from the year before. In sharp contrast to declining public school figures, enrollment in charter schools rose 4.5% to more than 52,000.\nIn 2022, there was roughly one teacher for every 14 students in a Wisconsin classroom, compared to the national average of 1:16. AAA State of Play considered Wisconsin to have the 14th best teacher to student ratio in the U.S.\nDistrict | City (main office) | Total Enrollment |\n---|---|---|\nMonroe School District | Monroe | 2,202 |\nBrodhead School District | Brodhead | 1,017 |\nNew Glarus School District | New Glarus | 957 |\nAlbany School District | Albany | 294 |\nMonticello School District | Monticello | 284 |\nJuda School District | Juda | 280 |",
